[gd_scene load_steps=9 format=3]

; A dead subsystem burning out of one part of a hull.
;
; Everything here is authored (CLAUDE.md 5.1). The script places, sizes, spins
; and fades these nodes; it never makes one.
;
; THREE PARTS, and the arrangement is the whole design:
;
;   Scar   a scorch mark lying flat on the plate, the mark that says something
;          under this spot is finished. disc.obj, not billboarded.
;   Flame  a broad base half sunk into the plate, a narrow tongue licking up
;          out of it, and a small white heart at the opening. The Y offsets and
;          relative scales below are the SHAPE of a flame, which is arrangement
;          and so belongs in the scene; how big the whole thing is drawn and
;          how fast it flickers are tuning and live in data/tuning.json
;          (CLAUDE.md 5.4).
;
;          The base and the heart sit at NEGATIVE Y, which is what puts them
;          inside the plating: fire coming out of a hull has to start below the
;          hull, or it reads as a fire standing on top of one.
;   Plume  twelve smoke puffs. top_level, so a puff stays at the world point it
;          was made at while the ship sails on: that is what turns a fire into
;          a trail without anything having to know the ship's velocity. Same
;          trick the drone's exhaust plume uses.
;
; Twelve, because the trail is only as long as the puffs it has: at the rate in
; data/tuning.json a ring of twelve is about three seconds of smoke, which is
; the puff lifetime, so the oldest puff is fading out just as its slot is
; wanted again. Eight recycled a puff that was still half bright, which cut the
; trail off in mid air.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/ui/subsystem_fire.gd" id="1"]
